<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-what-to-add-to-ramen">What To Add To Ramen</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The beauty of this recipe is that it&#8217;s a (very very) blank canvas. You can add whatever you would like to make it your own and zazz things up!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you want some direction, here are some options to think about:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://www.loveandlemons.com/how-to-make-soft-boiled-eggs/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Soft-boiled egg</a></li>



<li>Crunchy panko (see details in the FAQ below)</li>



<li>Scallions or chives</li>



<li>Sesame seeds</li>



<li>Toasted sesame oil</li>



<li>Corn</li>



<li>Bok choy</li>



<li>Chili oil </li>



<li>Nori (dried seaweed)</li>



<li>Gochujang and kimchi</li>



<li>Sriracha </li>



<li>Shredded chicken or thinly sliced beef or pork</li>
</ul>



<h2 class="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions: Homemade Ramen</h2>



<div class="schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block"><div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1615754134147"><strong class="schema-faq-question">How do I make the crunchy panko topping?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">To make crunchy golden panko crumbs, heat a few tablespoons of oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the panko, stir for one minute or less, or until golden brown. Remove and place on paper towels to drain. You can also toss the panko with a little oil and toast them in the oven to get them golden and crispy.</p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1615754200270"><strong class="schema-faq-question">I don&#8217;t like mushrooms. Can I leave them out?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Sure! You can swap just about any veggie in its place or leave them out entirely. We&#8217;d recommend still cooking with the mushrooms though to give the broth a nice umami flavor and then just remove the mushrooms before serving. </p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1615754290293"><strong class="schema-faq-question">How do I make the soft-boiled egg to go on top?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Good news &#8211; this is super easy! Boil water on the stove in a pot. Add your egg straight from the fridge and put the lid on the pot. Boil the egg for 6 minutes. Remove the egg and plunge it into an ice water bath. Peel the shell off, cut the egg in half, and place your beautiful jammy egg on top of your ramen.</p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1658335039392"><strong class="schema-faq-question">All I have is powdered broth. Can I use it?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Sure! Liquid broth levels up this recipe but you can skip the ramen seasoning packet and swap just about any powdered broth in its place. We like <a href="https://amzn.to/3PlvG0chttps://amzn.to/3PlvG0c" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener sponsored nofollow">this</a> powdered soup base. <em>(Affiliate link)</em></p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1658335673822"><strong class="schema-faq-question">My local grocery store didn&#8217;t have dried shitake mushrooms. Where can I find them?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Good news &#8211; you can order them online <a href="https://amzn.to/3yTjbSv" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow">here</a>. <em>(affiliate link)</em></p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1658336554603"><strong class="schema-faq-question">Have you used toasted sesame oil in this recipe? </strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">Yes, we’ve used both <a href="https://amzn.to/3vrHZQR">toasted sesame oil</a> and <a href="https://amzn.to/3PG0NDE" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow">regular</a>. <em>(affiliate links)</em></p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1726851653977"><strong class="schema-faq-question">What other vegetables are good in ramen?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">The kale and carrots are great here for texture and color, but I also love to use spinach, bok choy, and fresh mushrooms as well.</p> </div> <div class="schema-faq-section" id="faq-question-1726851729735"><strong class="schema-faq-question">Could I add meat to this ramen recipe?</strong> <p class="schema-faq-answer">You could add some pre-cooked and shredded chicken (rotisserie chicken works great here!), or throw in some shrimp near the end and let it cook in the broth.</p> </div> </div>



<br>



<section class="wp-block-wp-tasty-tasty-links-featured">
<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center" id="favorite-ramen-cookbooks">Favorite Ramen Cookbooks</h2>


	<article class="tasty-link-card">
