<li class="comment odd alt thread-odd thread-alt depth-1" id="comment-1066409">
	<article class="flow-root" itemprop="comment" itemscope="" itemtype="https://schema.org/Comment">
		<div class="comment-image">
			<img data-pin-nopin="nopin" loading="lazy" nopin="nopin" alt="Pinch of Yum Logo" src="https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e6f6596458ba94643657bcbbbe529eb646e1bc79a2ceb054f5f81b31cd7f7fc9?s=75&#038;d=https%3A%2F%2Fpinchofyum.com%2Fcontent%2Fassets%2Fimages%2Fpoy-avatar-grey-75x75.jpg&#038;r=g" srcset="https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e6f6596458ba94643657bcbbbe529eb646e1bc79a2ceb054f5f81b31cd7f7fc9?s=150&#038;d=https%3A%2F%2Fpinchofyum.com%2Fcontent%2Fassets%2Fimages%2Fpoy-avatar-grey-150x150.jpg&#038;r=g 2x" class='avatar avatar-75 photo' height='75' width='75' loading='lazy' decoding='async'/>		</div>
		<div class="comment-content">
			<div class="comment-author vcard" itemprop="author" itemscope="" itemtype="https://schema.org/Person">
				<meta itemprop="name" content="Abby"/>
				<cite class="fn">Abby</cite>			</div>
						<div class="comment-text w-full" itemprop="text"><p>Thank you for sharing this recipe!  My daughter wanted homemade ramen, so I searched online and the key word &#8220;quick&#8221; stood out to me as I am a working single mother.  I often use online recipes and I&#8217;ve never posted a comment before, but my 11 year old, 4 year old, and I agreed that this was the best ramen we&#8217;ve ever had, including from authentic restaurants!  It had the perfect amount of flavor and was definitely a &#8220;cozy&#8221; weeknight meal that will be in our regular rotation.  I made several changes because I either didn&#8217;t have the ingredients or I wanted to alter the flavor a bit:</p>
<p>-I used olive oil instead of sesame oil and minced ginger and minced garlic instead of grated.  </p>
<p>-I used fresh sliced baby Bella mushrooms instead of dried shiitake.  </p>
<p>-Instead of 4 cups water in the recipe, I used 4 cups vegetable broth.</p>
<p>-I added 1 chicken bouillon cube to the broth while it was cooking.  </p>
<p>&#8211; I added a bag of frozen mixed vegetables to the broth while cooking.  </p>
<p>&#8211; I added a little salt, pepper, soy sauce, garlic powder, onion powder, and soft boiled eggs at the end (along with the scallions and kale).</p>
<p>-I imagine it would be pair well with chicken, steak, or tofu and I might add red pepper flakes next time for some extra kick, though it is wonderful without it.</p>
</div><p class="tasty-recipes-ratings"><span class="tasty-recipes-rating tasty-recipes-rating-outline" data-tr-clip="100" data-rating="5"><svg role="presentation" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#wpt-star-full"></use></svg></span><span class="tasty-recipes-rating tasty-recipes-rating-outline" data-tr-clip="100" data-rating="5"><svg role="presentation" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#wpt-star-full"></use></svg></span><span class="tasty-recipes-rating tasty-recipes-rating-outline" data-tr-clip="100" data-rating="5"><svg role="presentation" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#wpt-star-full"></use></svg></span><span class="tasty-recipes-rating tasty-recipes-rating-outline" data-tr-clip="100" data-rating="5"><svg role="presentation" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#wpt-star-full"></use></svg></span><span class="tasty-recipes-rating tasty-recipes-rating-outline" data-tr-clip="100" data-rating="5"><svg role="presentation" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#wpt-star-full"></use></svg></span></p>
			<div class="comment-meta commentmetadata">
				<meta itemprop="datePublished" content="2026-07-28T19:26:30-05:00"/>
				<a href="https://pinchofyum.com/quick-homemade-ramen#comment-1066409">07/28/26 @ 7:26 pm</a>
											</div>
